---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import {projectsNewestFirst} from '../../lib/catalog';
const levels=['All','Beginner','Intermediate','Advanced'];
---
<BaseLayout title="ESP32 Projects & DIY Robotics Build Plans | MAKHEX" description="Browse 12 ESP32, electronics and robotics project blueprints with hardware BOMs, build steps, original-maker credits and MAKHEX component links.">
<section class="page-hero container"><span class="eyebrow">THE PROJECT SHELF / {projectsNewestFirst.length} IDEAS</span><h1>Make the<br/><em>next thing.</em></h1><div class="page-hero-bottom"><p>Find ESP32 beginner projects, wireless gadgets, electronics displays and advanced robot builds. Select a blueprint to see its bill of materials, proposed steps and verification notes.</p><span class="page-count">{projectsNewestFirst.length} hands-on ideas to explore</span></div></section>
<section class="container catalog-section"><div class="catalog-toolbar"><div class="filters" aria-label="Filter difficulty">{levels.map((level,i)=><button type="button" class:list={['filter-button',{selected:i===0}]} data-level-filter={level} aria-pressed={i===0}>{level}</button>)}</div><div class="toolbar-note">Starting ideas · lab testing still in progress</div></div>
<p class="reference-catalog-disclosure">New to ESP32? <a href="/blog/esp32-project-ideas/">Compare eight projects by difficulty, parts and engineering requirements.</a> Photos show independent makers' actual hardware, not a MAKHEX-assembled kit. Board revisions, firmware and parts may differ; inspect each credited source before building.</p>
<div class="project-grid projects-page-grid" id="projects-grid">{projectsNewestFirst.map(p=><div data-level={p.level}><ProjectCard project={p}/></div>)}</div>
<aside class="disclosure-box"><span class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU BUILD</span><h2>Blueprints, not finished kits.</h2><p>These are starting plans and have not been tested end-to-end on a fixed hardware bundle. Confirm board revisions, electrical limits and SDK dependencies before construction.</p></aside></section>
<script is:inline src="/scripts/filter-projects.js"></script></BaseLayout>
